schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: "GENIUS Act (July 2025) — first US federal stablecoin law"
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    In July 2025 the US passed the GENIUS Act, the first federal law for
    stablecoins, requiring fiat-backed issuers to hold genuine 1:1 reserves
    and publish a monthly reserve report checked by an independent
    accounting firm.
  evidence: >-
    Article cites a Latham & Watkins legal-explainer summary of the GENIUS
    Act in its References section.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/stablecoins.md
  interpretation: >-
    Presented as a trust-building regulatory development for fiat-backed
    stablecoins, giving "better-run coins" legal pressure to prove reserves.
  uncertainty: >-
    Legislative summary as reported by a law-firm explainer; not
    independently re-verified against the statute's text in this ingestion
    pass, and subject to future regulatory/implementation changes.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/stablecoins.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
